  where nothing survives a line is a much bigger defect than the dead code this
  phase removed, but fixing it means changing how the analyzer sees a REPL scope,
  which is not this phase's concern. → `FINDINGS.md` #1
- For the same reason `:vars` still lists only `_`: a `set` the session made is
  not a name the next line can read, so the listing has nothing else to show. The
  *ordering* half of `FINDINGS.md` #2 is fixed; the content half is the analyzer
  gap above.
- `ReplCompleter` is now constructed and reachable via `Repl::complete`, but
  `rb` never calls it: there is no readline binding, so the read loop still uses
